                "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                "username": "tifu_amdeng"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sathish Sekar",
                        "username": "sksekar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you share some sample event logs capturing the following scenarios:\n\n1. PowerRailFault with valid register & value\n2. PowerRailFault where the register decode failed\n\nAlso, did you try various reset scenarios (AC/DC/Host reboot/BMC reboot) to check if the newly added event logs doesn't storm the event log? May need to rate limit and/or de-dup to log only transitions."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Rex Fu",
                        "email": "Rex.Fu@amd.com",
                        "username": "tifu_amdeng"
                    },
                    "message": "Sorry for the delayed response.\n\nI reviewed the logging behavior again and updated the patch accordingly.\n\nOne clear duplicate case exists in the original setup: if HPM_PWR_FAIL remains asserted across a BMC reboot, INIT_HIGH can replay the same PowerRailFault during BMC init even though no new fault transition occurred. To avoid duplicate logging, I updated the trigger handling to remove INIT_HIGH and keep this path transition-based by triggering on RISING only.\n\nI also refined the CPLD fault handling so the script now distinguishes:\n- valid register/value -> logs the decoded fault-specific rail\n- register decode failure -> falls back to HPM_PWR_FAIL\n- CPLD read failure -> falls back to HPM_PWR_FAIL\n\nBelow are sample event logs from the updated behavior.\n\n1) PowerRailFault with valid register/value\n\n- Mocked registers:\n - I2C_0x35=0x02\n - all other checked registers set to their expected non-fault values\n\n- Script output:\n  <3> OPENBMC_MESSAGE_ID={\"xyz.openbmc_project.State.Power.PowerRailFault\":{\"FAILURE_DATA\":\"FM_PVDDCR_CPU0_P0_FLT Power Fault (reg 0x35 bit 1 value 0x02)\",\"POWER_RAIL\":\"/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/board/Anacapa_MB/FM_PVDDCR_CPU0_P0_FLT\",\"_SOURCE\":{\"COLUMN\":45,\"FILE\":\"../git/log_create_main.cpp\",\"FUNCTION\":\"int generate_event(const std::string&, const nlohmann::json_abi_v3_12_0::json&)\",\"LINE\":34,\"PID\":25487}}}\n  /xyz/openbmc_project/logging/entry/64\n\n- Redfish EventLog:\n  {\n    \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/LogServices/EventLog/Entries/64\",\n    \"@odata.type\": \"#LogEntry.v1_9_0.LogEntry\",\n    \"AdditionalDataURI\": \"/redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/LogServices/EventLog/Entries/64/attachment\",\n    \"Created\": \"2026-03-19T07:44:35.194+00:00\",\n    \"EntryType\": \"Event\",\n    \"Id\": \"64\",\n    \"Message\": \"A fault has been detected on power rail '/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/board/Anacapa_MB/FM_PVDDCR_CPU0_P0_FLT'.\",\n    \"MessageArgs\": [\n      \"/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/board/Anacapa_MB/FM_PVDDCR_CPU0_P0_FLT\"\n    ],\n    \"MessageId\": \"OpenBMC_StatePower.1.0.PowerRailFault\",\n    \"Modified\": \"2026-03-19T07:44:35.194+00:00\",\n    \"Name\": \"Manager Event Log Entry\",\n    \"Resolution\": \"None.\",\n    \"Resolved\": false,\n    \"Severity\": \"Warning\"\n  }\n\n2) PowerRailFault where the register decode failed\n\n- Mocked registers:\n - I2C_0x33=0x10\n - all other checked registers set to their expected non-fault values\n\n- Script output:\n  <3> OPENBMC_MESSAGE_ID={\"xyz.openbmc_project.State.Power.PowerRailFault\":{\"FAILURE_DATA\":\"Unknown Power Fault. CPLD decode failed reg 0x33 bits 4 value 0x10\",\"POWER_RAIL\":\"/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/board/Anacapa_MB/HPM_PWR_FAIL\",\"_SOURCE\":{\"COLUMN\":45,\"FILE\":\"../git/log_create_main.cpp\",\"FUNCTION\":\"int generate_event(const std::string&, const nlohmann::json_abi_v3_12_0::json&)\",\"LINE\":34,\"PID\":25350}}}\n  /xyz/openbmc_project/logging/entry/63\n\n- Redfish EventLog:\n  {\n    \"@odata.id\": \"/redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/LogServices/EventLog/Entries/63\",\n    \"@odata.type\": \"#LogEntry.v1_9_0.LogEntry\",\n    \"AdditionalDataURI\": \"/redfish/v1/Managers/bmc/LogServices/EventLog/Entries/63/attachment\",\n    \"Created\": \"2026-03-19T07:44:03.243+00:00\",\n    \"EntryType\": \"Event\",\n    \"Id\": \"63\",\n    \"Message\": \"A fault has been detected on power rail '/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/board/Anacapa_MB/HPM_PWR_FAIL'.\",\n    \"MessageArgs\": [\n      \"/xyz/openbmc_project/inventory/system/board/Anacapa_MB/HPM_PWR_FAIL\"\n    ],\n    \"MessageId\": \"OpenBMC_StatePower.1.0.PowerRailFault\",\n    \"Modified\": \"2026-03-19T07:44:03.243+00:00\",\n    \"Name\": \"Manager Event Log Entry\",\n    \"Resolution\": \"None.\",\n    \"Resolved\": false,\n    \"Severity\": \"Warning\"\n  }\n\nIn addition, if HPM_PWR_FAIL is asserted but no specific CPLD fault can be decoded from the checked registers, the script logs a generic fallback event:\n- \"Unknown Power Fault. HPM_PWR_FAIL asserted but no CPLD fault was decoded\"\n\nFor the reset scenarios:\n- AC cycle: HPM_PWR_FAIL is cleared after AC reset, so I do not see the same duplicate-log concern there.\n- DC cycle / Host reboot: these are not meaningful validation paths while HPM_PWR_FAIL remains asserted in this fault state.\n- BMC reboot: this was the clear duplicate case in the original setup, which is why INIT_HIGH was removed."
                }
            ],
